notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T16:54:01.451Z","harness:codex","Packing policy: direct endpoints remain in breadth-first producer order. Reserve their root-edge token costs before admitting more distant nodes and emit root-incident edges first. Tiny accepted packets and explicit edge/depth caps may still omit relationships; completeness and producer-bounds omission receipts must remain visible. Do not equate a full field projection with an unbounded traversal."
  "2026-10-21T17:33:48.823Z","harness:codex",Graph preflight linked the historical dependency-context comparison and the actual startup-admission investigation as related work. The unrelated GitHub issue census points directly to its already-reviewed PR instead of inventing an implementation relationship. The graph policy and exemption ledger are unchanged.
